---

20 — TESTABLE RULES

A-001 Action cannot execute without preview.
A-002 Preview must include consequence scope.
A-003 Denied action must expose explicit reason.
A-004 Executed action must emit proof reference.
A-005 Revoked authority must block new execution.
A-006 UI may not label unverified action as verified.
A-007 Review path must be reachable from execution record.

---

21 — PUBLIC / PRIVATE BOUNDARY

Public surfaces may show:
- action type
- public status
- public proof pointer

Restricted fields stay protected:
- private rationale
- restricted identifiers
- non-public dependencies

Metadata leakage is forbidden.

---

22 — THREE-SPEED PARTICIPATION

SPEED 01 — QUICK INTENT
Short, clear action choice.

SPEED 02 — INFORMED DECISION
Consequence and boundary explanation.

SPEED 03 — FULL INSPECTION
Proof, policy, lineage, review history.

User chooses depth.
System truth remains unchanged.

---

23 — CANONICAL FORMULA

«Participation is welcome.»

«Authorization is bounded.»

«Execution is attributable.»

«Proof is inspectable.»

«Review is available.»

«Revocation remains real.»

---

24 — FINAL RULE

Nothing may appear executable
if constitutional authorization is absent.

Everything that appears executed
must be traceable in proof.

